Hi [~accountid:608fb3be0b80a60069c7f299], apologies, I seem to have missed your replies in my Inbox. 

{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}
As an overarching comments, we are not opposed to your Team storing employee records in Box, as this is standard practice in many markets. We have a Data Processing Agreement in place with Box and they’ve been vetted and onboarded already :green-check: 
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
My concerns rather lie in some of the detail you’ve highlighted around _data retention_ (how long we retain data after our purpose for collecting it has expired) and _data scope_ — whether we’re collecting any data, especially sensitive data like medical records — when we shouldn’t. I’ve left questions about these aspects in bold below
{panel}

{quote}All employment records we collect from employees before and during the employment and all records that we create for the employment. This can include diplomas, previous work certificates, medical referrals, medical reports, employment contract and it’s annexes, termination agreement etc.{quote}

# *I want to flag that we should not be indefinitely retaining copies of Diplomas, Previous Work Certificates, etc, in hard copy or digitally, that were submitted as part of a job application after a Candidate has been rejected, or successfully accepted and offered a role. Does your Team have a process to delete these records once an employee has been onboarded and passed their probation?* 
# *What medical referrals/medical reports are being referred to here, and why do we hold them?* 

{quote}The we plan to audit the physical documents for current employees to make sure we have 100% all digitally available. Additionally all physical documents will be kept in the locked storage units in the Warsaw office as they are kept now.{quote}

*Please clarify whether we plan to permanently destroy all physical copies once we have created digital copies? If not, why are we retaining physical copies? Is there a company policy or local regulatory requirement to do this?* 

{quote}I believe this is from the _Regulation of the Minister of Family, Labour and Social Policy on employee documentation._ It was shared with us by the local People Partner.{quote}

As mentioned, Privacy does not review the security statute of our 3rd parties, or whether they meet specific security requirements. Please submit a ticket to the InfoSec Team to determine whether Box meets this requirements “_Provide encryption in transit and at rest, and ensure audit trails of all access and modifications (§6.1.2)_”

