Thank you for your additional comments and clarifications regarding this program.
It is very good that the details of the rewards program will be visible to drivers only and will not be public, publishing it in the driver app through the Bolt Rewards feature. This indirectly mitigates the risks associated with reclassification.

Generally, I do not consider that this program is not available. However, please note that given that there is no clarity how the Platform Workers Directive will be implemented in the local legislation in Sweden, at least until 31 December 2025 (discussions and investigations are still ongoing), we can not be completely sure that we will not be in need at some point of time to change the conditions of the program or even discontinue the program.

In any case, at the time being I would like to point out the following (in addition to the comments of Dan Erik Roosve under this ticket: [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-40764|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-40764|smart-link] ):

a) reward value should remain symbolic or token-base, not of sufficient value to influence work behavior or create financial dependence. It is recommended avoiding structuring rewards in a way that they could become a material part of a driver’s income;

b) when drafting the terms of the program or marketing the program or communicating the program to the drovers, it is very important to avoid employment-like or incentive-heavy language. Neutral, benefit-focused terminology shall be preferred, such as, “Bolt Rewards Access”, “Partner Benefit Offers”, “Driver Perks Program”;

c) it shall be ensured that participation in Bolt Rewards is optional and that opting in or out does not affect driver access to trips or other app functionality;

d) It is highly recommended not positioning the program as a reward for “hard work”, “dedication”, “loyalty” or “consistency”, language that resembles employment  performance review criteria.

Hope this helps. But if you have any further questions or require a clarification, please let me know. Thanks! 🙏

